1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
This is Wren — a research assistant that runs entirely in your terminal, through Claude Code.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Let me show you how you get started, from nothing, in about two minutes.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
You start with one command.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Wren scaffolds a fresh project, sets up its memory and its safety rules,

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
and checks everything installed cleanly.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
No accounts, no database, nothing external required.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Then you run one thing: /setup wren.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Instead of dropping you at a blank page, it gives you a short guided tour —

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
how your memory persists across sessions, the fourteen-phase path a paper takes,

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
and the rule that you never write prose until your analysis is frozen and checked.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
After the tour, it interviews you.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
What do you work on. What data you use. What you want to write.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
It's a conversation, one question at a time —

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
and it listens, so what you say shapes how the whole system is set up for you.

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
From your answers, it sets up the right tools.

16
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:27,000
A simple file store, or a real database if your data needs one. Your reference manager.

17
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Only what you'll actually use — matched to the work you described.

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
And you don't finish empty-handed.

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:43,000
It sets up your first paper — or plans out a whole series —

20
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:52,000
so the moment onboarding ends, you're already working on something real.

21
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,000
That's Wren. It's free, it's open source,

22
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:01,000
and you can start right now with: npm create wren.

23
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Everything you've seen is at rchoularton.github.io/wren.
